      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0151",
      "sequence": 163,
      "meaning": "The ocean of compassion gently accepts her subtle, beautiful boon, granting everything she desires and declaring that his grace will keep her extraordinary discernment from ever fading. Manu bows and adds one more request: let his attachment to the Lord’s feet be like a serpent’s dependence on its jewel or a fish’s on water, even if others call him foolishly possessive of his son. The Lord grants it and commands them to dwell for a time in Indra’s capital, enjoy its great pleasures, and then become king and queen of Ayodhyā, where he will be born as their son.",
