    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0152",
      "sequence": 164,
      "meaning": "The Lord promises to manifest in a lovingly fashioned human form in their home, assume bodies along with his portions, and perform deeds that give devotees joy; fortunate people who hear them reverently will cross worldly existence after abandoning possessiveness and pride. His primal Power, by whom the world was created, will also descend as his māyā. Repeating that he will fulfil their longing and that his pledge is utterly true, the Lord disappears. The couple cherish their gracious Lord, remain in the hermitage awhile, then effortlessly leave their bodies and dwell in Amarāvatī. Śiva concludes this sacred account and begins another cause of Rāma’s birth.",
