    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0153",
      "sequence": 165,
      "meaning": "Śiva tells the ancient, purifying tale of Kaikaya, where the world-renowned king Satyaketu lived, a pillar of righteousness and repository of policy, splendour, virtue and strength. His two heroic, battle-firm sons were abodes of every excellence: the elder crown prince Pratāpabhānu and the younger Arimardana, unmatched in arm-strength and immovable in war. The brothers’ mutual love was free from every fault and deceit. Giving the kingdom to his elder son, Satyaketu retired to the forest for Hari’s sake. Under Pratāpabhānu’s sunlike glory, Vedic rule and care for subjects prevailed everywhere without a trace of sin.",
