    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0154",
      "sequence": 166,
      "meaning": "Pratāpabhānu’s wise, benevolent minister Dharmaruci was comparable to Śukra; his brother Arimardana was mighty, while the king himself was a mass of splendour and resolute in battle. Delighting in his vast fourfold army and countless seasoned warriors, the king chose an auspicious day, sounded the drums and marched to conquest. After many battles he defeated all rulers by force, brought the seven continents under his power, accepted tribute, and restored their kingdoms. Thus Pratāpabhānu alone ruled the whole earth; returning triumphantly to his city after subduing the world, he enjoyed wealth, righteousness, desire and other goods at their proper times.",
