    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0155",
      "sequence": 167,
      "meaning": "Through Pratāpabhānu’s power the lovely earth became a wish-fulfilling cow: all suffering vanished and righteous men and women prospered. Dharmaruci, devoted to Hari’s feet and the king’s welfare, taught him sound policy. The king constantly served teachers, gods, saints, ancestors and Brahmins, joyfully performed every royal duty prescribed by the Vedas, and daily gave many kinds of gifts while hearing the finest scriptures, Vedas and Purāṇas. He built wells, stepwells, tanks, flower gardens, Brahmin dwellings, temples and varied holy places. With loving devotion he performed every sacrifice described in scripture thousands upon thousands of times.",
